**Connectivity diagram**

Hover over any component to see exactly what it connects to. The five connection types tell different stories:

Red (query path) — the hot path a user query takes: Channel → Kong → FastAPI → RLS Core Engine → LangGraph → LiteLLM → vLLM or Azure OpenAI. LangGraph also reaches into LlamaIndex → Qdrant for RAG retrieval, and directly queries PostgreSQL/ClickHouse for deterministic data.

Blue (data flow) — the ingestion pipeline: all 9 external sources feed through Airflow into the four storage engines (PostgreSQL, ClickHouse, MinIO/Iceberg, Qdrant). Debezium provides CDC into Redpanda for real-time streaming to ClickHouse.

Green (real-time API) — LangGraph agents calling external systems directly during query execution: SAP S/4HANA for live stock/pricing, Salesforce for CRM data, SharePoint for document retrieval, Asana for action tracking. These are the "tool calls" the agents make.

Amber (auth/security) — Entra ID feeds both Kong (authentication) and the RLS Core Engine (identity → scope resolution). OPA enforces policies at Kong. Guardrails AI + Presidio validate LLM inputs/outputs through LiteLLM.

Purple (monitoring) — LiteLLM reports to Langfuse (LLM observability). MLflow serves models to vLLM. Prometheus feeds Grafana. ClickHouse feeds Metabase for self-serve analytics. Evidently AI monitors model drift via MLflow.

