The updated connectivity diagram now shows all 35 components with the 4 new data quality components sitting between the pipeline layer and the storage layer. Hover over any of them to see how they connect:

Soda Core — connected to Airflow (orchestration), PostgreSQL, ClickHouse, and MinIO (validates data in all three storage engines at Bronze, Silver, and Gold checkpoints), and Grafana (quality metrics dashboards).

dbt Core — connected to Airflow (triggers dbt runs as DAG tasks), PostgreSQL, ClickHouse, and MinIO (executes Bronze→Silver→Gold transformations across all storage engines).

OpenMetadata — the most connected new component. Links to all four storage engines (catalogs and profiles every table/collection), Airflow (captures DAG lineage automatically), and Grafana (data quality dashboards visible in the monitoring stack).

LLM Enrichment — connected to Airflow (orchestrated as DAGs), LiteLLM (calls the LLM proxy for classification, entity extraction, quality scoring), and writes enriched results back to Qdrant (enriched embeddings with classification tags) and PostgreSQL (enriched metadata columns in Gold tables).

The green dashed lines are the new data quality flow connections — visually distinct from the existing blue (data), red (query/AI), amber (auth), and purple (monitoring) connection types. When you hover over Airflow, you can see it's now the central orchestrator for both the data pipeline AND the quality pipeline — exactly as designed, with zero new orchestration tools needed.